---
// /product — Stockwerk 1 (product\10 §4): was FixedR beim allerersten Trade tut.
// Der Reifegrad IST die Gliederung (Befund B, product\10 §1): "In the build today" und
// "On the way" sind zwei getrennte Gruppen, nicht eine Liste mit Sternchen.
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import PageHead from '../components/PageHead.astro';
import ReifegradChip from '../components/ReifegradChip.astro';
import StopShield from '../components/illus/StopShield.astro';
import Distribution from '../components/illus/Distribution.astro';
import Horizon from '../components/illus/Horizon.astro';
import LayoutMosaic from '../components/illus/LayoutMosaic.astro';
import RCalendar from '../components/illus/RCalendar.astro';
import PayoutLock from '../components/illus/PayoutLock.astro';
import DynamicRisk from '../components/illus/DynamicRisk.astro';
import Icon from '../components/Icon.astro';
import { FEATURE_PAGES, LANE_OF, LINE_OF } from '../content/produktnavigation';
---
<Base
  title="Product"
  description="What FixedR does the day you connect an account: mandatory stop-loss, position size from risk, R-only display, multi-account distribution, synchronised multi-timeframe layouts, and what's still being built."
  bare
>
  {/* H1/Eyebrow nach Kanvas 2026-09-02 ("Everything here starts working the day you
      connect an account." → "Two groups. Not a feature list with asterisks."). Der
      Absatz bleibt: er trägt den Querverweis auf /methodology, den das Kanvas nicht
      abbildet — s. Protokoll. Runde 13 (FXR-142): jetzt im Kopfband (PageHead). */}
  <PageHead eyebrow="What it does on your first trade">
    Two groups. Not a feature list with asterisks.
    <Fragment slot="lede">
      This is the first of two things FixedR does. The mechanics below run today — no setup
      beyond connecting your accounts. The second layer, the process that carries you across
      months rather than a single trade, lives on <a href="/methodology">Methodology</a>.
    </Fragment>
  </PageHead>

  <div class="wrap">

  {/* ── Nabe (FXR-239) ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
      Acht Kacheln auf die acht Feature-Seiten. Sie stehen VOR den beiden
      Reifegrad-Gruppen, nicht statt ihnen: die Nabe verteilt, die Gruppen darunter
      erklären, was heute läuft und was entsteht. Damit hat das Aufklappbanner in der
      Kopfleiste ein Ziel, das keine der acht Seiten ist.
      Inhalt aus content/produktnavigation.ts — dieselbe Quelle wie Banner und
      Fußzeile, damit die Liste nicht an drei Orten gepflegt wird. */}
  <section style="padding-top: 2.5rem; padding-bottom: 0;">
    <div class="section-head">
      <p class="eyebrow">Eight pages, one cockpit</p>
      <h2>Where each part of it lives.</h2>
      <p>
        The mechanics on this page are the short version. Each of the eight below goes into one
        part of the cockpit properly — what it does, how it behaves, and where its limits are.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="hub-tiles">
      {FEATURE_PAGES.map((p) => (
        <a class="hub-tile" href={`/product/${p.slug}`}>
          <span class="ic"><Icon name={p.icon} size={20} /></span>
          <span class="t">{p.title}</span>
          <span class="d">{LINE_OF[p.slug]}</span>
          <span class="lane">{LANE_OF[p.slug]}</span>
        </a>
      ))}
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- In the build today — Gruppenkopf nach Kanvas: H2 + Pille statt Eyebrow + Zweit-H2. -->
  <section style="padding-top: 2.5rem;">
    <div class="group-head">
      <h2>In the build today</h2>
      <span class="reifegrad reifegrad-built">built</span>
    </div>

    <div class="feature-row">
      <div class="illu-box"><StopShield /></div>
      <div>
        <h2>Place the trade <ReifegradChip id="mandatory-stop" /></h2>
        <p>
          No stop, no trade — the constraint is structural, not a habit you keep or break.
          Risk is fixed before entry, not renegotiated with yourself while the position runs.
        </p>
        <p>
          Position size follows from that same stop: you set the risk, FixedR computes the
          size from the stop distance. <ReifegradChip id="position-size-from-risk" />
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="feature-row flip">
      <div class="illu-box"><Distribution /></div>
      <div>
        <h2>Across your accounts <ReifegradChip id="across-accounts" /></h2>
        <p>
          One order, sent to the accounts you choose, sized correctly for each. And a hard
          promise: <strong>without configuration, nothing is guessed</strong> — an
          unconfigured account stops the distribution with a loud error instead of quietly
          doing something almost right. MetaTrader and NinjaTrader sit under one surface.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="feature-row">
      <div class="illu-box"><Horizon /></div>
      <div>
        <h2>Read it in R <ReifegradChip id="r-only-display" /></h2>
        <p>
          Open positions, closed results, drawdown headroom — every number is denominated in
          R, never in currency. No money mode, no toggle to peek.
        </p>
        <p>
          Your month reads as a calendar of R values, comparable across accounts and account
          sizes: scale from a 10k account to a 100k and the calendar reads exactly the same —
          that's the point.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="feature-row flip">
      <div class="illu-box"><LayoutMosaic /></div>
      <div>
        <h2>Your working surface <ReifegradChip id="multi-timeframe-sync" /></h2>
        <p>
          The same symbol on several timeframes at once, each chart tile carrying a role you
          assign — <span class="r-value">HTF</span>, <span class="r-value">MTF</span>,
          <span class="r-value">LTF</span>. The synchronisation follows the role, not the
          window position — that is what turns an arrangement of charts into a named analysis
          structure. Layouts save that way, and alerts carry a target.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="illu-box" style="margin: 1rem 0 3rem;"><RCalendar /></div>

    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card">
        <div class="illu"><PayoutLock /></div>
        <h3>Protect the payout <ReifegradChip id="payout-lock" /></h3>
        <p>Once an account is eligible for a payout, trading on it can pause until you've
          taken the money out. Every other risk tool protects you from a loss; this one
          protects a win.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="card">
        <div class="illu"><DynamicRisk /></div>
        <h3>Risk that follows a rule <ReifegradChip id="dynamic-risk-rule" /></h3>
        <p>One R doesn't have to be the same fraction forever. Let it follow the state of the
          account, written down as a rule in the account profile — not decided in the
          moment.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="card">
        <h3>On your machine <ReifegradChip id="on-your-machine" /></h3>
        <p>A Windows application with an installer. No cloud account, no browser tab to
          leave open. What that does and doesn't mean for your data is on
          <a href="/trust">Trust</a>.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- R1: die Lage statt eines Produktvergleichs (product\10 §2 R1, D6.1) -->
  <section class="alt">
    <div class="wrap" style="padding: 0;">
      <div class="section-head">
        <p class="eyebrow">Without FixedR</p>
        <h2>What most of this replaces</h2>
        <p>
          Not a list of competitors — a list of what a prop trader does today, and where each
          approach runs into the same wall.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="grid cols-2">
        <div class="card">
          <h3>Checking balances in the broker terminal or firm dashboard</h3>
          <p>
            It gives you the firm's binding number — but it has no relationship to your own
            R record, so money and process live in two disconnected systems.
          </p>
          <p><ReifegradChip id="r-only-display" /> Read everything in the same unit, on the
            same screen you trade from.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="card">
          <h3>Enlarging a stop-loss by hand once the trade is open</h3>
          <p>
            It keeps a losing trade alive a little longer — and quietly turns "−1R maximum
            loss" into an open money scale, which is exactly the thing calm trading depends
            on not happening.
          </p>
          <p><ReifegradChip id="mandatory-stop" /> That door doesn't exist inside FixedR.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="card">
          <h3>Several single-purpose tools, no thread between them</h3>
          <p>
            Charts, indicators and a journal all exist somewhere already. What's missing is
            the connection between them — nothing forces the chain from definition to
            measurement to verdict.
          </p>
          <p><ReifegradChip id="across-accounts" /> One order ticket, one record, across
            every platform and account you trade.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="card">
          <h3>Watching the news calendar yourself and reacting by hand</h3>
          <p>
            It gives you full control — and no net if you don't react in time. The response
            depends entirely on you noticing and moving fast enough.
          </p>
          <p><ReifegradChip id="news-protection" /> An escalation ladder is on the way — see
            below. Netz, kein Garant. A net, not a guarantor.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- On the way — Gruppenkopf nach Kanvas: H2 + Pille statt Eyebrow + Zweit-H2. -->
  <section>
    <div class="group-head">
      <h2>On the way — and what shapes it</h2>
      <span class="reifegrad reifegrad-planned">planned</span>
    </div>
    <div class="section-head">
      <p>
        This is not a hedge. Building these with the first traders who use FixedR is the
        point of the founders circle — the record below is honest about what still needs to
        be built, and that's the invitation, not a caveat.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="grid cols-2">
      <div class="card">
        <h3>Automatic trade documentation <ReifegradChip id="auto-documentation" /></h3>
        <p>The plan sitting next to the result, without typing it up after the fact.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="card">
        <h3>Firm rule profiles <ReifegradChip id="firm-rule-profiles" /></h3>
        <p>Maintained rule sets per prop firm, instead of numbers you enter by hand.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="card">
        <h3>News protection <ReifegradChip id="news-protection" /></h3>
        <p>An escalation ladder around high-impact news. <strong>Netz, kein Garant.</strong>
          A net, not a guarantor.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="card">
        <h3>The monthly guardian statement <ReifegradChip id="guardian-statement" /></h3>
        <p>What the tool quietly prevented over a month, laid out the way a statement is.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="callout">
    <p>
      FixedR is a Windows application, works with MetaTrader &amp; NinjaTrader, and is built
      exclusively for prop-firm accounts. <a href="/waitlist">Join the waitlist →</a>
    </p>
  </section>
  </div>
</Base>
